<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Privacy Policy | MileageLogMaker', description: 'What MileageLogMaker does with your data: trips saved in your browser, details sent to build your PDF and not kept, Gumroad license checks and who gets data.', canonical: SITE + '/privacy' }) %>
</head>
<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="lead">MileageLogMaker has no accounts, no cookies, no analytics and no advertising. This page lists the data the site handles, where it goes and why.</p>
  <p class="lead">Last updated: 15 October 2026</p>
</section>
<article class="content">
  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>MileageLogMaker (www.mileagelogmaker.com) is run by Peak Apps Studio. For any question about your data, email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>Trips you enter</h2>
  <p>The trips you add to a mileage log are saved in your browser's local storage, so the list is still there when you come back. US, Canadian and UK logs are saved separately. The mileage reimbursement calculator saves its own trip list in the same way and does all its sums in your browser. When it hands trips over to the log generator, they travel in the part of the link after the # sign, which browsers do not send to servers.</p>
  <p>Your trips stay on your device until you delete them in the tool or clear this site's data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>When you download a log or an export</h2>
  <p>When you download a PDF log, or a CSV or Excel export with Pro, your browser sends the log to our server, which builds the file. The request contains your trips (dates, start and end places, purposes, distances and trip types), the name and vehicle you entered, odometer readings, the tax year and region settings, and, if you have Pro, your license key and your logo.</p>
  <p>The server builds the file in memory, sends it back to your browser and does not keep a copy. If a file fails to build, the server writes a technical error message to our hosting logs.</p>

  <h2>Pro license checks</h2>
  <p>When you enter a Pro license key, it is saved in your browser's local storage so that Pro stays on in that browser. The key is sent to our server when you activate it and with each Pro download, and the server checks it with Gumroad's license service (api.gumroad.com) to confirm that it belongs to a purchase that has not been refunded. After a successful check, the server keeps the result, with the email address on the purchase, in its memory for up to six hours. It does not write them anywhere else.</p>

  <h2>Where you came from</h2>
  <p>When you open the site, it notes what kind of site sent you, as one word such as "google", "ai-assistant", "social", or "direct" when no site did. A tag in the address you arrived at, such as the utm_source=chatgpt.com that ChatGPT adds to its links, counts before the site you came from. The word for this visit is kept in session storage and deleted when you close the tab; the first word other than "direct" is also kept in local storage until you clear this site's data. Only the word is kept, never the address of the page you came from, and it goes nowhere unless you click a buy button.</p>

  <h2>Buying Pro</h2>
  <p>Pro is sold through Gumroad. The buy button opens Gumroad's checkout, where you give your payment details to Gumroad, not to us. As the seller, we receive your email address and the details of your order from Gumroad, and we use them to answer questions about your purchase and to issue refunds.</p>
  <p>When you click a buy button, the link to Gumroad carries three labels: the word for the kind of site you came from (the first one kept in your browser, or else this visit's), its group (search, referral, social or none) and the name of this site. Gumroad stores them with the sale, so we can see which kinds of sites bring buyers: a search engine, an AI assistant, Pinterest, a social network, another website or none. Gumroad learns only the kind of site, never its address.</p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site runs on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel processes each request, including your IP address, the page you asked for and your browser type, and keeps request logs for a limited time. The site uses your device's own fonts, so no font service sees your visit.</p>

  <h2>Emails</h2>
  <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and your message. Mail sent to peakappsstudio.com addresses is forwarded by Forward Email to a Gmail inbox. We use your email only to reply to you.</p>

  <h2>Who else receives data</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data fit">
    <thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>What for</th><th>Privacy policy</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Vercel</td><td>Hosting the site and its server</td><td><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" rel="noopener">vercel.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Gumroad</td><td>Checkout, payments and license checks, and the kind of site you came from when you click a buy button</td><td><a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy" rel="noopener">gumroad.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Google</td><td>The Gmail inbox for our email</td><td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Forward Email</td><td>Forwarding mail sent to our address</td><td><a href="https://forwardemail.net/en/privacy" rel="noopener">forwardemail.net</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Vercel, Gumroad and Google are based in the United States, so your data may be processed there. We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Trips and your license key in your browser: until you delete them or clear this site's data.</li>
    <li>The word for the kind of site you came from: until you close the tab, and the first one until you clear this site's data.</li>
    <li>Details sent to build a PDF or export: only while the server builds the file.</li>
    <li>License check results and the purchase email: up to six hours in the server's memory.</li>
    <li>Hosting logs: kept by Vercel for a limited time under its own policy.</li>
    <li>Purchase records: kept by Gumroad under its own policy.</li>
    <li>Emails: until we delete them. Ask us and we will delete yours, unless we need it as a record of a payment or refund.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a> and we will reply within one month. Most of the data this site uses never reaches us: you can delete your trips yourself in the tool or by clearing this site's data. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>MileageLogMaker is a tool for drivers who claim business mileage and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the site starts handling data differently, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Peak Apps Studio, <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
</article>
